    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reworked `nextCustomerCode`:\n- Now takes `city` and `lastName`.\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city, `LAST3` = upper-cased first three of the last name.\n- `NNNN` is now a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence: one more than the count of existing owners already in that city (case-insensitive match), instead of one more than the global owner count.\n- Updated the call site and Javadoc accordingly (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007`).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) already derives from `customerCode`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format; I only updated the Javadoc example to `SYD-SMI-0007-M26` to stay accurate.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`, passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
